  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.0": "The American Red Fox is a medium-sized,",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.1": "quadrupedal, omnivorous mammal native",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.2": "to North America. It is a subspecies",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.3": "of the European Red Fox. It inhabits",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.4": "a wide range of habitats, from dry",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.5": "brushlands to snowy forests, but are",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.6": "more common in temperate forests and",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.7": "grasslands. It is a somewhat solitary ",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.8": "animal, living either alone until mating,",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.9": "or in small family groups made of a",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.10": "leading mated pair and their offspring,",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.11": "and usually the female is the leader of",
  "screen.project_wildlife.creature_compendium.irl_info.american_red_fox.12": "the group.",


